<details id="website-analytics" class="analytics-preference">
  <summary>Website analytics settings</summary>
  <div class="preference-content">
    <p>
      May we use Fastlane to understand visits from our social posts? If you allow
      it, Fastlane saves visitor and session IDs in your browser and receives
      page addresses, the referring site, screen size, language, time spent and
      scroll depth. This is only for this marketing site, not your BeFree account.
    </p>
    <p class="status" data-analytics-status role="status" aria-live="polite">
      Fastlane analytics are off until you allow them.
    </p>
    <div class="choices">
      <button type="button" data-analytics-allow disabled>Allow Fastlane</button>
      <button type="button" data-analytics-deny disabled>Keep Fastlane off</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      You can change this here any time. Turning it off clears its browser IDs
      and reloads an active page. Vercel’s existing cookie-free audience measurement
      is separate. <a href="/privacy#website-analytics">How website analytics work</a>.
    </p>
    <noscript><p>JavaScript is off, so Fastlane will not load.</p></noscript>
  </div>
</details>

<aside id="fastlane-consent-prompt" class="consent-prompt" aria-label="Optional website analytics" hidden>
  <h2>Help us understand what brings you here?</h2>
  <p>
    Optional Fastlane analytics saves visitor and session IDs in your browser
    and measures visits from our social posts. It starts only if you allow it.{' '}
    <a href="/privacy#website-analytics">Privacy details</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="status" data-analytics-status role="status" aria-live="polite">
    Fastlane analytics are off until you allow them.
  </p>
  <div class="choices">
    <button type="button" data-analytics-allow disabled>Allow Fastlane</button>
    <button type="button" data-analytics-deny disabled>No thanks</button>
  </div>
  <p class="note">You can change this any time in the website footer.</p>
</aside>

<script>
  import { initFastlaneAnalytics } from '../lib/fastlane-analytics.js';
  initFastlaneAnalytics(window);
</script>

